Canvas Deadline Agent Personal Learning License
Version: 1.0-review-draft (2026-10-23)
Public project attribution: Breathe4me

REVIEW DRAFT — NOT EFFECTIVE

This is a proposed custom source-available license for rights-holder and legal
review. It grants no new permissions until the rights holder expressly approves
and identifies an effective final version. Preparing or publishing this draft
does not make its proposed permissions effective. Existing separate permissions,
applicable statutory rights and independent third-party licenses are unaffected.
The legal rights holder, ownership of covered material and licensing contact
remain to be confirmed. Breathe4me is public attribution, not a verified legal
identity or a representation of ownership of all included material.

This is not an MIT, Apache or OSI-approved open-source license. The proposed
terms below describe the intended personal-use and separate-authorization model.

1. Scope and definitions

"Licensor" means the rights holder to be identified in the final agreement.
"Application" means only the original Canvas Deadline Agent code, interface
assets and documentation that Licensor owns or is authorized to license. It
excludes third-party software, course content, user data and third-party marks.

"Personal Learning Use" means a natural person's own noncommercial study and
learning. A student managing their own coursework at a school or university is
a personal user. Enrollment alone does not authorize deployment by the school.

"Institutional Use" includes managed deployment or operation for a school,
class, university, nonprofit, public body or other organization. "Commercial
Use" includes enterprise operations, resale, commercial hosting, paid services
and using the Application to provide paid tutoring or other services.

2. Proposed free personal-use permission

Subject to an effective final agreement and compliance with its terms, Licensor
proposes a nonexclusive, worldwide, royalty-free permission to run and inspect
the Application, make private modifications and compile a personal copy solely
for Personal Learning Use. No enrollment documents are required by this policy.
This permission would cover application licensing only; it does not waive fees
or terms imposed by Canvas-related services, AI providers or PushPlus.

3. Institutional and commercial authorization

Institutional and Commercial Use require separate prior written authorization.
Nonprofits may apply for free authorization but have no automatic exemption.
An inquiry, silence, payment without an agreed license, or public availability
of source code does not constitute authorization. See COMMERCIAL_LICENSE.md.

4. Copies, modifications and redistribution

Retain applicable copyright, license and attribution notices in permitted
copies. Clearly identify modifications and do not present an unofficial build
as an official release. Permission for private modification and compilation
does not grant permission to redistribute modified installers, portable builds,
commercial bundles or hosted services. During Beta, no third-party permission
to redistribute modified installers is granted by default.

Additional rights to publish modified source or mirror unmodified binaries
remain subject to express final approval; no such additional grant is made by
this draft. Linking to an authorized official download is not hosting a copy.
Nothing here restricts viewing, forking or other rights independently required
by GitHub's applicable terms for content placed in a public repository. Those
platform rights do not create an unrestricted institutional or commercial grant.

5. Third-party materials

Third-party materials retain their own licenses. This agreement neither
relicenses them nor places a noncommercial restriction on rights their owners
grant independently. Their applicable terms govern those materials in a
conflict. Preserve their required notices, license texts and source availability.
Consult THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the license/source materials supplied with
the particular distribution; a notice alone does not prove redistribution rights.

Any upstream-required modification, redistribution, reverse-engineering or
library-debugging rights remain intact, including an applicable WebView2 SDK
NOTICE exception. Applicable Microsoft distributable-code restrictions must
also be satisfied. No permission to copy arbitrary Windows system files or
claim Microsoft endorsement is granted. The final agreement must be checked
against the exact upstream terms for the files actually distributed.

6. Ownership, accounts and security

No ownership, trademark rights or institutional endorsement is transferred.
Use only accounts, tokens, local files and course data you are authorized to
access. This license does not authorize access-control bypass or attacks on
third-party systems. Good-faith, nondestructive inspection of lawfully obtained
copies in an authorized isolated environment is within the proposed inspection
permission; no third-party legal immunity is promised.

External contributions require an explicit rights review and agreed terms
before acceptance. Submitting a contribution does not automatically assign
copyright or establish a right to license someone else's work.

7. Data, external services and Beta limitations

Read PRIVACY.md for data handling. The Application does not submit coursework
automatically. Local completion is not Canvas-confirmed submission. Official
Canvas records remain authoritative; complete deadline coverage, notification
delivery and suitability for any course are not guaranteed. Third-party
services have separate terms and charges. AI is optional and uses your own key.

8. Proposed warranty and liability terms

To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Application would be provided
AS IS and AS AVAILABLE, without warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
particular purpose or noninfringement. No maintenance, availability, support
response time or future compatibility is promised absent a separate agreement.

Any final limitation of liability, including treatment of missed deadlines,
data loss and consequential loss, requires express approval and legal review.
No monetary liability cap, indemnity or exclusion of non-excludable rights is
established by this draft. Mandatory consumer protections and other rights that
cannot lawfully be excluded remain unaffected.

9. Finalization, prior rights and reserved decisions

Before effectiveness, confirm the legal rights holder and ownership provenance,
contact, final license identifier and date; resolve source-publication and
binary-redistribution permissions, borderline paid/donation-supported use,
termination and cure, patent treatment, governing law and dispute procedure;
and approve warranty/liability wording and upstream contractual exceptions.
No jurisdiction, compulsory arbitration or patent-retaliation policy is chosen.

Termination must not revoke independent third-party rights or authorize deletion
of user data. A later license must not silently replace permissions already
granted for an earlier version. The review history and unresolved questions are
documented in docs/LICENSE_SOURCE_AVAILABLE_DRAFT.md; neither draft grants an
operative application license. Publishing source, approving this license and
authorizing a public binary release are separate decisions.
